<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dalmau de Queralt, Count of Santa Coloma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1640</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Count of Santa Coloma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dalmau de Queralt, Count of Santa Coloma, was a Catalan noble who served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of Catalonia for Philip IV. Enforcing the billeting of royal troops, he became hated, and he was killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-de-sang">Corpus de Sang</a> riot of 7 June 1640, which began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reapers-war">Reapers' War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dalmau-de-queralt-count-of-santa-coloma.jpg" alt="Dalmau de Queralt, Count of Santa Coloma" width="320" height="485" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dalmau_de_Queralt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
